docs/DECISIONS.md:3103:- The deep read of the v94 draws ($0; `design-v72.md` §11 holds the lists, each checked against the article or the raw answer): (1) 42 of the 148 supporting matters never reach the judge in any draw and 30 are never written at all: other companies' and partners' actions and figures with a path to the company (a memory maker's revenue and a customer's price rises, a rival's customer forecasts, a supplier's expansion, partners' adoption of the company's products) and analysts' scenario numbers; the closing check's rows "another company's matter when you cannot say through which path", "product detail" and "arrangement in place" remove what standard 5.1 kinds 2 and 3 keep (D240); v73's examples recovered about two a draw. (2) Of the five core matters never written, one is a scorer miss (the compute-framework retelling is written in other words and filed), four are real: an analyst's view that consensus is too low and a capex forecast in one note, "Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy these processors" (a policy fact inside a background sentence), and the four-die to two-chiplet design change (written under role-v53, dropped since v66 as a product detail). (3) About half of the statements filed under the Data Center revenue question are not evidence of it (one reader, 20 sampled: 6 right, 3 under the wrong question, 11 ecosystem or partner lines, a reactor demonstration, a market estimate), and the company's own blog posts supply most of them; 24% of the written noise is still the dated retelling. (4) The extraction links an open question's own estimates only when they name the question's period or population: 3.7 core and 14.3 supporting statements a draw are written and dropped for no home with the question open (the $20 billion CPU target against the Vera CPU question in 2 of 3 draws; 82% and 41% growth against total revenue; the $1 trillion Blackwell and Rubin figure). (5) The shown list suppresses proposals: the Ohio guarantee question, in the judgement gold, opened in one draw of three (two of three under the placement architecture); the operating-margin and capex seeds never receive a statement and are never judged. (6) Smaller: the remaining quote refusals (6–10 a draw) are paraphrases the model writes instead of copying a comparison sentence; two or three of fifteen sampled statements carry a doubtful tier (an author's commentary stored as fact). Nothing of this is built; the order and the fixes are proposals in §11.
docs/DECISIONS.md:3105:## D268 · 2026-11-02 · The first prompt audit's six fixes, each a contradiction or a missing example in the request, built as extraction v75 / poc-v95 and proved on stored data; the run is Alex's call
docs/DECISIONS.md:3107:- Alex, after the audit table (`design-v72.md` §12, the first run of `.claude/skills/prompt-audit`): "1 到 6 都改，存档证明，然后放到一起我再决定跑不跑". The audit's verdicts, one per failure class: (1) the closing check's row 7 ("another company's matter when you cannot say through which path …") contradicts the role's kind 2 (a supplier's, customer's, competitor's or partner's action with a size bears on the company by that relation); (2) the role's reject-list clause keeps "a partner's or customer's adoption or integration" with no condition while kind 2 requires a size, date or name; (3) the T8 category block's "forecasts and price targets with their figures" contradicts D240, the check's row 1 reads an undated policy decision as background, and row 3's boundary has no example of a design change; (4) the T6 block (company publications) names "partnerships" and nothing says a company's own list of partners, users or showcases is not evidence; (5) the figure questions' takes line "estimates and revisions for X over <period>" and the role's "a different period is another question" contradict the links field's "bars no figure from another period when no open question covers it"; (6) "copy its quote verbatim" has no example for a comparison sentence that starts with the other company.
docs/DECISIONS.md:3110:- Status: poc-v95 is built and proved on the stored requests; it is not the default (poc-v94 stays, D267) and no draw is sent until Alex decides. What the proofs do not show: the whole-bench effect (three draws) and the two classes left wanting, the 23 supporting matters still never written (the model's conservatism on other companies' figures outlives the sentence) and the comparison-sentence quotes.
docs/DECISIONS.md:3113:## D269 · 2026-11-03 · The second prompt audit, on the v95 draw: the one large class left is a precedence contradiction; the sentence-level fix (v77) is a patch and is not kept; the next step is structural
docs/DECISIONS.md:3119:## D270 · 2026-11-03 · The structural fix built three ways (v78, v79, v80): the keep decision as closed-set fields the model fills and code applies; what it carries and what it does not; a whole-bench draw of poc-v100 against v94 proposed, Alex's call
docs/DECISIONS.md:3121:- Alex (00:20): "去你妈的你给我继续工作。那你跑这个skill到底结构性要怎么改才能让harness这个agent做我想要的事情according to PRD; don't drift". Built on the audit's conclusion (D269): each evidence item classifies itself in closed sets the schema defines in the standard's own words with examples from other industries, and `extraction.evidence_rule` applies the standard's keep rule to that classification; the role's reject list and the end-of-request check are gone from v78 on. Three versions, each proved on the same two stored sets (the 29 articles holding the 41 supporting matters v94 reached in at most one draw; 11 blog, comparison and core-miss articles holding 41 core and supporting matters), three sends each, counted after the sift as what reaches the ledger, every answer saved (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/sends/poc-v*.json`) so a recount costs nothing (`resend_targets.py --replay`): v78 / `poc-v98` (party, news, scale), v79 / `poc-v99` (the standard's first question, "is this new information?", as its own field first; every statement of a kind written, new or known), v80 / `poc-v100` (the kind "view" for a general view with no new fact; the newness definition sharpened where the model's own account showed it stretched). Record: `design-v78-fields.md`.
docs/DECISIONS.md:3123:- What the classification carries: a class the model recognizes as a shape and is told to write (an old figure, an arrangement in place, a market move, a product comparison, a view) it labels honestly and code drops with a reason: 249 of v80's 738 statements on the 29 articles. What it does not carry: whether an asserted claim is common knowledge (standard 5.1, D243 item 5): the model's own account on five probes (`probe-v79-newness.txt`, `probe-v80-common-knowledge.txt`) calls an asserted claim with figures or dated changes "new" every time, and no definition sentence moved that across three versions. v78's own lesson: a field on a written item records the model's decision unless the walk asks for every statement (v78: 21 not-kept labels in 1,017 statements; v79 with "write the known ones too": 17%; v80: 27%).
