s "direct drivers … with a size" clause removed no noise and cost 11 core or supporting homes. The noise that reaches is seven tenths under the credit-support programme's questions, routed there by D207's "names that matter" rule; only the extraction can stop it (D252's paired examples, role-v65, measured at the extraction layer only). The calls: (a) make `placement-narrow-v2` the placement prompt, with its clause "when the question's market and period cover them" cut (the placer's own account names it for dropping a core share statement; D240's principle); (b) generate the seeds from `poc/universe.json`'s watch list by code and have the analyst add the driver questions the list lacks (EPS root, competition and share including China, the programme as a deal question), Alex signing the list before anyone reads the window's articles; (c) the order R1 seeds → R2 D248 items 2–3 in matching identity → R3 role-v65 end to end, each with a $0 proof on stored requests first. Done on his word to start the work (2026-10-31 night, loop log row 69): R1's second seed file (`poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json`, 23 questions with provenance, `design-seed-v2.md` with the $0 proof and frozen predictions) and its three replays, which stopped on day 1 with Jev HTTP 402 (the account's credit; only Alex restores it; the folders `poc/data/e2e-v83-seedv2-d1..3` resume with their run.sh); R2's census, design, $0 replay and code on branch `fix/question-identity-r2` (worktree `hivemind-identity-r2`; `design-r2-identity.md` §5), measured after R1. R3's first step (2026-11-01, loop log rows 70–71, `design-r3-review.md`): of the ten core or supporting statements that reach judgement under role-v53 and role-v65's stored draws keep in at most one, the model's own account traced one to a rule, the closing check's views row ("a quote that only characterises") dropping a company's denial of a reported delay; role-v66 (`poc-v84`; role and categories identical to v65, `review-v66.txt` adds one boundary to that row, the company's own statement that its plan, schedule or guidance still stands is judged as the plan itself would be; two Codex audits; `extraction.REVIEW_UNTIL` 65 → 66) was sent on the whole bench, three draws against the stored v65 draws: the denial 1/3 → 3/3 and an unseen denial of the same kind 0/3 → 2/3, none of the 17 guard noise statements re-admitted in two draws, core every draw 72 → 70 and supporting 122 → 120 inside the two-send noise floor, gold-rejected kept 59.3 → 60.7; the per-statement flips (22 new, 17 gone) are at the scale of two sends of one prompt (8 and 21). R3's end-to-end arm therefore uses role-v66 in place of v65, after R1 and R2, and needs Jev credit. Open for Alex: R2-c (the collision judge no longer overrides a code identity) and R2-d (figure-question duplicates: one plan's wordings, growth against level, GAAP against non-GAAP). The default stays role-v53 / `poc-v69` (placement v1, no seeds) until he decides; a switch names its `poc` config in `scripts/replay.py`, the default-entry test and the README, and is recorded. After these: D248 items 2–3 in matching identity (11 of 30 questions a draw opens are one bet under another deadline or milestone), then the record-field class (F1–F8) and opening (O1–O9).

The handoff plan with every open task, the principles and the quantitative criteria is [`handoff-plan-2026-10-30.md`](research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/handoff-plan-2026-10-30.md).

**Evidence bloat, before anything else downstream:** not solved, reduced at the source. The window rule (D198, judging-v5) hides old pieces by recency, not by count: in the sealed three-month ledger the largest judging request after it (Data Center revenue) still showed 647 pieces (1,185 hidden), 93,634 input tokens, because a broad thesis took 40–60 new links a day. Placement under the one-home rule (D207–D209) cut the first week's links per item 3.3 → 1.82 and the largest thesis's links 106 → 52, the largest judging request 15,229 → 8,649 tokens (`english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28` against the sealed ledger's same week), measured over one week with role-v22 only. The decisive test is the whole-pipeline run over the three-month window with `poc-v69` (on Alex's go, with a cap), read for links per thesis, the largest judging request and any halt; the structural answer, a versioned argument record per question for the judge to read, is designed nowhere yet (handoff plan T6).

## Parallel day (D172–D183)

The replay runs the parallel day by default (D183: Alex chose it to converge faster); `scripts/replay.py --workers 1` runs the serial path, needed to resume a day a serial run left unfinished. Measured live on the complete July 27 day (53 items), three serial against three parallel trials interleaved ([result](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/results.md)): median 501.8 s → 112.5 s, **4.46× end to end**, 5.91× for item work; daily judging (~37–40 s) is the same code in both modes. Every trial's audit is clean; each parallel trial's runner accepted exactly the rebuilt exact-prefix request for all 53 items; each trial's answers replayed through the other mode give an identical ledger. Drift from the recorded sequential golden is inside the serial trials' own spread. The product entry point (`--workers 16`) ran the same day live in 135.5 s with the same checks clean. On recorded answers the parallel day equals the golden in all ten tables (D180, and again on the promoted module).

Fifteen consecutive days (August 1–15, 221 items) with every call answered by one deterministic oracle of the request bytes, at no cost (D182, [result](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-multi-day-oracle/results.md)): the parallel ledger equals the serial one in all 20 product tables, its turns accepted exactly the serial run's 221 extraction requests, and a broken runner was caught. At recorded call durations the fifteen days take an estimated 2.79× less time (2,512 s → 900 s); a busy day gains 3.6–4.5×, a day of a few items 1.5–2×.

What remains of the time is not scheduling: items that depend on the item just before them (~45–60 s), daily judging (D63), and each item's two matching phases in order (~17 s). Ten times end to end on this day would need those to shrink.

