r":"fact","event_time":"Announced June 2026","links":["v9","v20"]},{"id":"e6","quote":"Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027.","one_line":"SharonAI guided that its footprint would reach 132MW, including 102MW contracted, and its total NVIDIA GPU count would exceed 55,000, including the 40,000 backstopped GB300s, by mid-2027.","speaker":"SemiAnalysis","original_who":"SharonAI","original_day":"","tier":"party_statement","event_time":"By mid-2027","links":["v20"]},{"id":"e7","quote":"Firmus’ 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.","one_line":"Firmus announced a 360MW AI cluster in Batam, Indonesia, backed by NVIDIA, on June 29, 2026; SemiAnalysis said it would likely be housed in a DayOne facility.","speaker":"SemiAnalysis","original_who":"Firmus","original_day":"2026-06-29","tier":"fact","event_time":"Announced 2026-06-29","links":["v9","v20"]},{"id":"e8","quote":"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years. We expect a portion of the revenue above the backstop level will be shared with Nvidia as per the structure we outlined earlier today.","one_line":"Firmus announced expected customer revenue of $25 billion to $30 billion over six years for its project; SemiAnalysis expected a portion of revenue above the NVIDIA backstop to be shared with NVIDIA.","speaker":"SemiAnalysis","original_who":"Firmus","original_day":"2026-06-29","tier":"party_statement","event_time":"Six years","links":["v9","v20"]},{"id":"e9","quote":"Beyond this – Firmus also announced a 600MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor that will also underwrite 1.2GW of new renewables development and 1.5GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032. Firmus will still need to identify a datacenter provider or build their own datacenters before they can deploy GPUs.","one_line":"Firmus announced a 600MW firm-energy deal with Gunvor to underwrite 1.2GW of new renewables development and 1.5GWh of storage in South Australia by 2032; it still needed a data-center provider or to build its own before deploying GPUs.","speaker":"SemiAnalysis","original_who":"Firmus","original_day":"","tier":"fact","event_time":"By 2032","links":["v20"]}],"candidates":[],"new_groups":[]}

